hta['1_1_3'] = '{3:1:1:3}<htaDiv_3><tr class="HTAnote"><td>NOTE These subscriptions, though found in many manuscripts, in some of the best as in the Vatican, are shorter in form, and in the Sinaitic and Alexandrian are wholly wanting. Furthermore, as Paley has said, six of them at least are either false [as 1 Corinthians, Galatians, 1 Timothy] or improbable [as 1 Timothy, 2 Timothy and Titus]. There is some reason for supposing that they were added by Euthalius, bishop of Sulci, in Sardinia, who flourished between 450 and 600 A.D. -H.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'Rom\', 16, \'-\');">Rom 16<\/a> Written to the Romans from Corinthus, and sent by Phebe servant of the church at Cenchrea.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'1Cr\', 16, \'-\');">1Co 16<\/a> The first epistle to the Corinthians was written from Philippi by Stephanas, and Fortunatus, and Achaicus, and Timotheus.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'2Cr\', 13, \'-\');">2Co 13<\/a> The second epistle to the Corinthians was written from Philippi, a city of Macedonia, by Titus and Lucas.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'Gal\', 6, \'-\');">Gal 6<\/a> Unto the Galatians written from Rome.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'Eph\', 6, \'-\');">Eph 6<\/a> Written from Rome unto the Ephesians by Tychicus.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'Phl\', 4, \'-\');">Phl 4<\/a> It was written to the Philippians from Rome by Epaphroditus.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'Col\', 4, \'-\');">Col 4<\/a> Written from Rome to the Colossians by Tychicus and Onesimus.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'1Th\', 5, \'-\');">1Th 5<\/a> The first epistle unto the Thessalonians was written from Athens.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'2Th\', 3, \'-\');">2Th 3<\/a> The second epistle to the Thessalonians was written from Athens.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'1Ti\', 6, \'-\');">1Ti 6<\/a> The first to Timothy was written from Laodicea, which is the chiefest city of Phrygia Pacatiana.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'2Ti\', 4, \'-\');">2Ti 4<\/a> The second epistle unto Timotheus, ordained the first bishop of the church of the Ephesians, was written from Rome, when Paul was brought before Nero the second time.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'Tts\', 3, \'-\');">Tts 3<\/a> It was written to Titus, ordained the first bishop of the church of the Cretians, from Nicopolis, of Macedonia.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'Phm\', 1, \'1-1\');">Phm 1<\/a> Written from Rome to Philemon, by Onesimus a servant.<\/td><\/tr><tr class="HTAnote"><td><a  onClick="return multiVerse(\'Hbr\', 13, \'-\');">Hbr 13<\/a> Written to the Hebrews from Italy by Timothy.<\/td><\/tr><\/table><\/div><htaTail>';
